# Review

The title makes a contestable claim about what explicit retention provides. A commitment can be legible yet distributed across several rules, examples, or procedures. An informed reader could therefore argue that making the commitment explicit still leaves the learner without a direct target for revising it. The title asserts that explicit retention supplies such a target. The note treats the effect of an edit on later behavior as a separate question to test.
